                <pb facs="0667" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg581"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Combs.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-03-24"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis instructs Mr. Combs to protest-against the unfriendly action of the
                    Guatemalan Government in refusing to recognize the American citizenship of
                    Posadas, who was duly naturalized in the United States after a residence of
                    twelve years, and to ask for Posadas’ release.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
